G-M3 — MiniVic first-token latency, baseline on live (before this lane's deploy)
Measured 2026-09-05 ~13:09Z from the VPS (srv1356245). Live: https://forgotten-mistory.web.app

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. POST /api/chat through Firebase Hosting — the payload the client actually sends
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Note on method: the payload in the task's VERIFICATION block ({"message","mode","history"})
is not the shape lib/miniVicBrain.ts puts on the wire. The function's
normaliseConversation() requires `messages`, so that payload returns 400 without
ever reaching a provider and would have measured nothing. Every number below uses
the real shape.

  $ P='{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"What did Vikram do at the ATO?"}],"mode":"hiring"}'
  $ for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do curl -s -o /dev/null \
      -w '%{time_starttransfer} %{time_total} %{http_code}\n' \
      -X POST https://forgotten-mistory.web.app/api/chat \
      -H 'content-type: application/json' -d "$P"; done

  4.178278 4.178425 200      <- cold instance
  2.016016 2.016197 200
  1.392391 1.392474 200
  2.080699 2.081759 200
  1.797195 1.797271 200

  n=5   P50 2016 ms   P95 (nearest-rank) 4178 ms   best 1392 ms
  warm only (n=4): P50 1907 ms
  Budget: < 1500 ms. FAIL.

  time_starttransfer == time_total on every trial: nothing arrives until the
  whole answer is finished. That is the shape of a buffered, non-streamed reply
  and it is what the reviewer measured from the browser (P50 2121 ms).

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. Where the time goes — the ladder rungs, measured not assumed
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The hypothesis handed to this lane was that a cold instance pays a failing
OpenRouter rung before a working rung answers, costing "~0.5-1 s of the budget".
Measured directly against each provider (keys read by name from
/root/.claude/.env.production with a grep reader; no value printed):

  openrouter  POST /api/v1/chat/completions  -> http=402 in 0.169 s
              {"error":{"message":"Insufficient credits", ...}}

  So the rung tax is REAL but it is ~0.17 s, not 0.5-1 s. Reordering the ladder
  cannot on its own bring 2016 ms under 1500 ms. The hypothesis is half right:
  the rung is dead, but it is not the budget.

  deepseek    non-streamed -> http=402 in 1.174 s ("Insufficient Balance")
              streamed     -> http=402 in 0.654 s
  The local DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is also out of balance. The DEPLOYED function
  answers 200 with real grounded text, so Secret Manager holds different (working)
  credentials for at least one rung — which rung answers in production is now
  recorded per request by this lane's rung-timing log line, rather than guessed.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. Cold start
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
First send after an idle period: 4178 ms vs ~1900 ms warm — roughly 2.3 s of the
first visitor's wait is container start. `firebase functions:log` confirms the
pattern: "Starting new instance. Reason: AUTOSCALING" appears before each idle-period
send, and the STARTUP TCP probe succeeds ~1.0 s later.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. /api/tts (the voice half of R3) — reviewer's correction confirmed
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Not re-measured in this lane; the reviewer's 2026-09-05T13:06Z correction stands:
POST /api/tts -> 200 audio/mpeg, 36.8 kB, 0.395 s. The deployed ElevenLabs secret
is a valid key; only the local .env.production copy is a key ID. No blocker here.
